    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="0792" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.–Subs/4: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-15T13:00:00-05:00">June 15, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. In response Department’s circular of June 13, 8 p.m., Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="19a" xml:id="d855-f1"/> says Ecuador has complied with
                    all recommendations Inter-American Neutrality Committee: Ecuadoran decree No.
                        12<anchor n="20" xml:id="d855-f2"/>
                    <pb facs="0793" n="781" xml:id="pg781"/> covers submarines, 15<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d855-f3"/> internment and No. 19<anchor n="22" xml:id="d855-f4"/>
                    merchant ships and auxiliary vessels.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d855-f1" n="19a" xml:id="d855-f1-content">
